## Course overview

Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches at Higher Level is for students who enjoy the elegance of mathematics and the power of abstract reasoning. It places a strong emphasis on **algebraic manipulation, proof, and calculus**, and prepares students for university study in mathematics, engineering, physical sciences, and economics.

## What you will study

- **Number & algebra** — sequences, series, binomial theorem, proof, and complex numbers (HL).
- **Functions** — transformations, polynomials, rational, exponential, and logarithmic functions.
- **Geometry & trigonometry** — identities, equations, vectors, and 3D geometry.
- **Statistics & probability** — distributions, the binomial and normal distributions, and Bayes' theorem (HL).
- **Calculus** — limits, differentiation, integration, differential equations, and Maclaurin series (HL).

## Assessment

| Component | Weighting | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 | 30% | No calculator |
| Paper 2 | 30% | Calculator allowed |
| Paper 3 | 20% | Extended problem-solving (HL) |
| Internal Assessment | 20% | The Mathematical Exploration |

## The Exploration

The IA is a 12–20 page **Exploration** — a piece of independent mathematical writing on a topic of your choice. It is assessed on presentation, mathematical communication, personal engagement, reflection, and the use of mathematics. The best Explorations connect mathematics to something you genuinely care about.
